---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout title="Shared WebAssembly loading">
<p class="eyebrow">Browser · Flutter · Rust</p>
<h1>Prepare the bytes.<br/>Keep the runtime in charge.</h1>
<p class="lead">Reusable preparation, caching and activation across product organizations, with release-specific Flutter bootstrap and Rust glue.</p>
<a class="button" href="/adopt/">Adopt the loaders</a>
<a href="https://github.com/ores-wasm-loaders/owls-docs">Read the source and documentation ↗</a>
<div class="flow" aria-label="Loading stages"><span>01 / Validate release</span><span>02 / Prepare public assets</span><span>03 / Verify bytes</span><span>04 / Activate explicitly</span></div>
<div class="grid"><article class="panel"><h3>One release contract</h3><p>Independent TypeSpec and JSON Schema authorities are admitted through TJSV. Host policy adds runtime-specific checks. <a href="/packages/#contracts">Follow the contract boundary.</a></p></article><article class="panel"><h3>Native extension points</h3><p>TypeScript adapters, Dart interfaces and Rust traits let each product own policy, transport, storage and startup.</p></article><article class="panel"><h3>Measured boundaries</h3><p>Review the exact component revisions, browser results and remaining device gates before adoption. <a href="/testing/">Inspect the evidence and its limits.</a></p></article></div>
</Layout>
